<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

    <!--
      Emergency Assistance is the one feature in this app that asks for FINE location,
      and it is a deliberate departure from the coarse-only stance the rest of the app
      takes (see core/platform and app manifests, where coarse is explicitly enough for
      the 2 km nearby-places radius).

      The reason is that this feature directs a real person to walk to another real
      person. The server buckets distance to 100 m at the closest band and shows a walking
      ETA off it. A coarse fix can be off by a kilometre or more, so "within 100 m, 2 min
      walk" computed from one would be a confident number that is simply wrong, and a
      wrong number is worse than no number when someone is waiting for help.

      Coarse is still declared and still requested alongside it. If she grants only
      coarse, the flow keeps working: the buckets widen and the ETA gets vaguer, which is
      the honest degradation. Nothing here requires background location, and the app never
      tracks her when a session is not active.
    -->
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION" />
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.ACCESS_COARSE_LOCATION" />

</manifest>
